# TrekViewer Environment Configuration
#
# NOTE ON CLIENT CREDENTIALS:
# Because TrekViewer is a framework-free client-only WebXR static application,
# any token configured here is loaded into the user's browser runtime and is visible
# in client network requests. A .env file DOES NOT make client-side credentials secret.
#
# For production deployments:
# 1. Register for a free token at https://cesium.com/ion/
# 2. In your Cesium Ion account dashboard, restrict token allowed domains/URLs to your origin
#    (e.g., https://your-domain.github.io or https://localhost:5173).
# 3. If no token is provided, TrekViewer automatically falls back to Esri World Imagery
#    and USGS Topo maps with zero setup or configuration required.

# Optional: Cesium Ion API Access Token for Microsoft Bing Aerial Photography
# VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=your_cesium_ion_token_here
